## Backend Checks

```bash
cd backend
uv sync
uv run ruff check .
uv run pytest
```

## Auth Development

The backend ships with starter auth routes under `/api/v1/auth`. Password reset
and email verification links are logged by the backend in local development.

```bash
devstack logs backend
```

Look for `auth.email.local_link` in the backend logs. That event includes the
verification or reset `link`.
{% if "mailhog" in services %}

This project also has MailHog enabled:

- UI: http://localhost:{{ ports.mailhog_ui }}
- SMTP inside Docker: `mailhog:1025`

The generated backend env is already wired to send local auth emails to MailHog.
{% else %}

MailHog is not enabled. If you want a browser inbox for local auth emails, run:

```bash
devstack add mailhog
```
{% endif %}

### Roles

Registered users default to `role = "user"`. The starter `/admin` route requires
`role = "admin"`.

Promote your first local admin from the project root:

```bash
devstack db shell
UPDATE users SET role = 'admin' WHERE email = 'you@example.com';
```

{% if frontend == "nextjs" -%}
The frontend starter pages live in `frontend/src/app/` and use the generated
auth client in `frontend/src/lib/auth/`.
{% elif frontend == "react" -%}
The Vite starter app lives in `frontend/src/App.tsx` and uses the generated auth
client in `frontend/src/lib/auth/`.
{% endif %}

## Docker Workflow

Use the global DevStack command from the project root:

```bash
devstack up
devstack logs
devstack down
```

Use the `Makefile` when you want shorter aliases.

## Environment

`backend/.env` is generated for the selected services. `backend/.env.example`
shows the full set of supported variables.

Do not commit real secrets.
